    <string name="step_notifications_text">Shows when BetterAuto is connected to the car, with a button to send the audio there.</string>
    <string name="step_media_title">Music access</string>
    <string name="step_media_text">Shows what\'s playing on the car screen and on the dashboard, and lets you control it. Turn on BetterAuto in the list.</string>
    <string name="step_audio_title">Music through the car speakers</string>
    <string name="step_audio_text_todo">Allow audio access so the music plays in the car.</string>
    <string name="step_audio_text_ask">Works now, but Android asks for permission every time you connect. To skip it, run this once from a computer:</string>
    <string name="step_audio_text_done">All set: the music goes to the car by itself when you connect.</string>
    <string name="step_audio_text_shizuku">All set, through Shizuku: the sound moves to the car with no prompt and no screen-sharing icon.</string>
    <string name="step_android_auto_title">Android Auto turned off</string>
    <string name="step_android_auto_text_todo">Android Auto is on and takes over the car connection. Open its page and tap Disable. If your phone doesn\'t allow it, run this from a computer:</string>
    <string name="step_shizuku_title">Shizuku (optional)</string>
    <string name="step_shizuku_purpose">With Shizuku, BetterAuto moves the phone\'s sound to the car like the official Android Auto: no permission prompt, no screen-sharing icon, the phone speaker is not muted, and apps that block copying play too. With the USB cable it needs a rooted phone: without root, Shizuku stops as soon as the phone connects to the car, and BetterAuto goes back to copying the sound.</string>
    <string name="step_shizuku_text_missing">Without it the sound is copied, with those limits. Shizuku is free on the Play Store.</string>
    <string name="step_shizuku_text_stopped">Installed but not running: open it and start it. Without root it stops after every restart of the phone and every time the phone connects to the car by cable.</string>
    <string name="step_shizuku_text_allow">Running: allow BetterAuto to use it.</string>
    <string name="step_shizuku_text_ready">Running, and BetterAuto is allowed to use it.</string>
