    <string name="settings_start_section_desc">Where I left off: the section you were in last time. Home: always the home screen.</string>
    <string name="settings_home_layout_desc">How many widgets the home screen shows: one big one, two side by side, or one big and two small.</string>
    <string name="settings_home_widgets_desc">What each place of the home screen shows. In the car you can also hold a widget to change it.</string>
    <string name="settings_widget_calendars_desc">Which of the phone\'s calendars the calendar widget shows. New calendars show up by themselves.</string>
    <string name="settings_weather_car_desc">Which weather app and which place: chosen in the BetterAuto app on the phone.</string>
    <string name="settings_theme_desc">Day or night colors. Auto follows the car\'s headlights signal, or the phone when the car doesn\'t send it.</string>
    <string name="settings_app_bar_desc">Where the bar with the sections goes. Auto: on the left on wide screens, at the bottom on narrow ones.</string>
    <string name="settings_rail_layout_desc">Order of the bar\'s buttons, which ones share a group and which are hidden. In the car you can also hold a button of the bar.</string>
    <string name="settings_clock_desc">The time in the top bar. Like the phone: 24 or 12 hours as on the phone (or as the chosen date formats use).</string>
    <string name="settings_date_desc">The date next to the time in the top bar.</string>
    <string name="settings_bell_desc">The bell in the top bar: how many notifications are waiting, and a tap opens them.</string>
    <string name="settings_auto_play_desc">When the car connects, the music you were listening to carries on by itself.</string>
    <string name="settings_bar_apps_desc">Music apps with their own button in the app bar. In the car you can also hold an app\'s button to pin or unpin it.</string>
    <string name="settings_unknown_audio_desc">Also sends the car the sound of apps that don\'t say what it is (a few players do). Off avoids stray sounds.</string>
    <string name="settings_quiet_mode_desc">No notification pop-ups while driving; they still collect behind the bell.</string>
    <string name="settings_notification_privacy_desc">Shows only who wrote and with which app. Auto: hidden while the car says someone else is aboard.</string>
    <string name="settings_notification_apps_desc">Which apps\' notifications show in the car. Apps appear here after their first notification.</string>
    <string name="settings_muted_chats_desc">Chats you muted from a notification in the car. Remove one to hear from it again.</string>
    <string name="settings_contact_names_desc">How names are written and sorted in the phone section and in calls.</string>
    <string name="settings_notification_groups_desc">Notifications from group chats. Hide them to see only messages written to you.</string>
    <string name="settings_voice_desc">Call and send messages by voice, with the steering wheel\'s voice button or the microphone button.</string>
    <string name="settings_voice_microphone_desc">Which microphone hears you. Auto: the car\'s when it has one, otherwise the phone\'s.</string>
    <string name="settings_voice_replies_desc">The answers are also spoken through the car\'s speakers, like \"Calling Mario Rossi\".</string>
    <string name="settings_mic_button_desc">A button in the top bar that starts voice commands, besides the steering wheel\'s voice button.</string>
    <string name="settings_units_desc">Kilometres and bar, or miles and psi, on the vehicle screens. Auto: as the phone\'s region uses.</string>
    <string name="settings_temperature_unit_desc">°C or °F for temperatures. Auto: as the phone\'s region uses.</string>
    <string name="settings_engine_light_desc">A warning light in the top bar while the car reports fault codes; a tap shows them with their meaning.</string>
    <string name="settings_smart_home_car_desc">Connect your smart home and choose its devices in the BetterAuto app on the phone.</string>
    <string name="settings_debug_desc">Technical details over the car screen (frame rate, connection, audio), for troubleshooting.</string>
    <string name="settings_weather_desc">Which weather app\'s widget the car shows. Auto picks one by itself.</string>
    <string name="settings_voice_language_desc">The language voice commands are heard and answered in. Auto: among the phone\'s languages, the one of the SIM\'s country.</string>
    <string name="settings_formats_desc">How dates, times and numbers are written in the car. Auto: the phone\'s language for the SIM\'s country.</string>
    <string name="settings_exlap_desc">Extra vehicle data from VW, Audi, SEAT, Škoda and Porsche head units, shown in the car under Vehicle.</string>
    <string name="settings_smart_home_desc">Gates, lights and scenes on the car screen, and buttons that show up when you arrive.</string>
